    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a difficult slate today as our offensive ceiling is heavily constrained by an elite matchup against Tarik Skubal. Our highest-rated play is **Gary Sanchez**, who earns a marginal 41.65 efficiency score. While Skubal\u2019s 2.85 xERA presents a significant hurdle, **Gary Sanchez** benefits from a positive platoon split and an assumed #5 spot in the order, which mitigates some of the SP skill penalty. Conversely, **Christian Yelich** sits at a 38.62, falling just below our threshold for a confident start. While **Christian Yelich** gains a nominal boost due to Skubal\u2019s slow delivery\u2014offering a slim window for a stolen base\u2014the severe L/L platoon disadvantage makes him a difficult sell despite his profile.\n\nThe benching of our primary assets, including **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, and **Trea Turner**, is necessitated by today's league-wide off-day, which limits our active pool to only these two representatives. Because we are prioritizing game cap preservation, we are not forcing starts for players like **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Caleb Durbin**, or **Kazuma Okamoto** in their absence. We are keeping a close watch on **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Colt Keith**, and **Lars Nootbaar** for future deployment, alongside depth pieces like **Hector Rodriguez**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez**. With Skubal on the hill, the primary risk remains a sub-par performance from **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich**; if the official lineups shift them lower in the order, we may see their efficiency scores dip further toward the floor.",
